entry.summary:
Most CSV ingestion scripts are written in 30 minutes. Most ingestion failures take 3 months to notice. The problem isn’t CSV. The problem is missing guarantees. In small teams, CSV ingestion often looks like this: Read file Loop rows Insert into database Print “Done” It works. Until the export format changes. Here’s what most ingestion scripts get wrong. Many scripts assume the column order never changes. That assumption eventually breaks. Instead of trusting positional mapping, validate headers explicitly: EXPECTED_HEADERS = [ "date", "customer_id", "amount", "currency", "status" ]
if headers != EXPECTED_HEADERS: raise ValueError("Schema mismatch detected")
Order-sensitive comparison is intentional. If upstream changes, ingestion should stop immediately. Silent d…
